   "description": "Weakness is the condition of being without sufficient strength to accomplish what is needed — the experience of one's own limitation and insufficiency. The Greek vocabulary here (astheneia) covers physical, moral, and spiritual weakness. In the New Testament, weakness is reframed rather than merely lamented: Paul's discovery is that God's power is most clearly visible in human weakness, that the strength that matters is not one's own. Weakness in this frame is not a problem to be solved but a condition to be inhabited honestly, which creates the space for divine strength.",
